name: Direct configuration coverage distinguishes enabled rules and inspected files
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_iac_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run iac-scan:scan {"target":"selected","kind":"all"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_iac_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART all
require-live-snap: 30 iac-scan: 2 findings | all-rules
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | opened-finding
submit: decision deferred Owned policy metadata requires owner review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_iac_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 inspected files | scoped-report
expect: Displayed Scan: completed
expect: paths selected
expect: paths selected · 2
expect: does not establish complete repository coverage
ask: Does Report show the selected directory and two inspected files without implying complete repository coverage or a verified vulnerability?
submit: logs
submit: run iac-scan:scan {"target":"selected","kind":"dockerfile"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_iac_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART docker
paste-file: @ART/docker-compare.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 1 not reassessed | disabled-family
expect: 0 not observed
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
resize: 160x48
live-snap: comparison-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: comparison-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: comparison-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: comparison-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: comparison-40x12
expect: 1 not reassessed
ask: Across six sizes, is the comparison readable and does it distinguish the excluded workflow file from the Dockerfile that was reassessed?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: logs
submit: run iac-scan:scan {"target":"empty","kind":"dockerfile"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_iac_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART empty
paste-file: @ART/empty-compare.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 2 not reassessed | empty-scope
expect: 0 not observed
keys: Escape
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-after-empty
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | restarted-review
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_iac_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: After no-color restart, are all three finite direct jobs, the exact scope and the earlier deferral retained with no model calls or source execution?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
